  "track": "Strings",
  "difficulty": "easy",
  "topics": ["strings", "hash-maps"],
  "source": "canonical Valid Anagram concept; description, examples, and tests re-authored",
  "description": "Return True if the strings s and t are anagrams of each other, meaning they contain exactly the same characters with the same counts, and False otherwise. Comparison is case sensitive: a and A count as different characters.",
  "constraints": [
    "0 <= len(s), len(t) <= 20000",
    "s and t consist of printable characters"
  ],
  "parameters": ["s", "t"],
  "functionName": "is_anagram",
  "starterCode": "def is_anagram(s, t):\n    # Return True if s and t contain the same characters with the same counts.\n    ...\n",
  "examples": [
    {
      "input": { "s": "listen", "t": "silent" },
      "output": true,
      "explanation": "both strings contain the same six letters"
    },
    {
      "input": { "s": "rat", "t": "car" },
      "output": false,
      "explanation": "s contains a t but t does not, so the counts differ"
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Two strings are anagrams exactly when every character appears the same number of times in both.",
    "A dictionary keyed by character can count occurrences in one pass.",
    "Count the characters of s, then decrement while walking t; if a count would drop below zero, or the lengths differ, answer False."
  ],
  "solution": "Compare lengths first, since different lengths can never be anagrams. Count each character of s in a dictionary, then walk t decrementing counts; any character missing or exhausted returns False, and surviving the walk returns True. One pass over each string: O(n) time, O(k) space for k distinct characters.",
  "solutionCode": "def is_anagram(s, t):\n    if len(s) != len(t):\n        return False\n    counts = {}\n    for ch in s:\n        counts[ch] = counts.get(ch, 0) + 1\n    for ch in t:\n        if counts.get(ch, 0) == 0:\n            return False\n        counts[ch] -= 1\n    return True\n",
  "bruteForceCode": "def is_anagram(s, t):\n    remaining = list(t)\n    for ch in s:\n        found = False\n        for i in range(len(remaining)):\n            if remaining[i] == ch:\n                remaining.pop(i)\n                found = True\n                break\n        if not found:\n            return False\n    return len(remaining) == 0\n",
  "failureHint": "hidden tests include empty strings, repeated characters, and one very long anagram pair",
  "parTimeSec": 300,
  "expectedComplexity": { "time": "O(n)", "space": "O(n)" },
